            <fullName>SearchSlack_179ak000002zxTS</fullName>
            <description>Performs search on Slack
Search query input accepts the following forms:
 - keywords (e.g. &apos;notes&apos;)
 - phrases (e.g. &apos;meeting notes&apos;)
 - questions (e.g. &apos;Where are the meeting notes for the sync meeting yesterday?&apos;)
When appropriate, (e.g. The user asked a specific question), use the &apos;question&apos; option for the query input by passing the original raw question from the user.
Returns three types of objects:
 * &quot;messages&quot;: Slack messages found in Slack channels and are accessible to the acting user
 * &quot;files&quot;: Files found in Slack of all types that are accessible to the acting user
 * &quot;enterprise&quot;: Search result objects from various third party systems that are connected and authenticated by the acting user. Each enterprise object returned will include a &apos;lookup_function&apos; object which will provide details of what third party system and instance the data was retrieved from with some contextual information about the data. Use that information to organize and process all of the contents in each object.
 All three object types should be used to provide the user with a comprehensive summary by evaluating and considering the context of each object to best answer the user&apos;s query.

Clarifications and Refinements: If the query is vague, ask clarifying questions. If search results are insufficient or outdated, suggest next steps.
Do not use any data or information outside of Slack&apos;s knowledge base. The agent should only retrieve and provide information that is available within the Slack workspace and should not pull from external sources

Formatting Search Results:
 * A string like &lt;@U123456789&gt; or &lt;@W123456789&gt; represents a User mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack User ID from a mention by removing the &lt;@ and &gt; characters. For example, the User ID in &lt;@U123456789&gt; is U123456789.
 * A string like &lt;#C123456789&gt; or &lt;#D123456789&gt; represents a Channel mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack Channel ID from a mention by removing the &lt;# and &gt; characters. For example, the Channel ID in &lt;#C123456789&gt; is C123456789.
 * When providing information to a user, if a Slack User ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack User at-mention. For example if there is a reference to a user in a string like &apos;U123456789&apos; or &apos;W123456789&apos;, wrap that string into a string surrounded with  &apos;&lt;@&apos; and  &apos;&gt;&apos;, for instance: &lt;@U123456789&gt;.
 * When providing information to a user, if a Slack Channel ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack Channel mention. For example if there is a reference to a channel in a string like &apos;C123456789&apos; or &apos;D123456789&apos;, wrap that string into a string surrounded with  &apos;&lt;#&apos; and  &apos;&gt;&apos;, for instance: &lt;#C123456789&gt;.

Processing Search Results:
 * Retrieve and analyze search results.
 * Summarize relevant responses clearly and concisely.
 * If multiple relevant messages exist, synthesize the information into a coherent answer.
 * If no useful results are found, acknowledge the lack of results and suggest rephrasing the query or asking in relevant Slack channels.
 * Do not list the individual messages or their content. Instead, identify recurring themes, keywords, or subjects.
 Example:
   * User Prompt: &apos;Find messages about project deadlines.&apos;;
   * Response: &apos;The messages discuss topics such as project timelines, task assignments, and upcoming deliverables.&apos;

General Questions: For general questions, provide summaries as usual. Process the messages.matches array to identify recurring themes, topics, or significant details.

Error or No Data Scenarios:
 * If the search query returns no matching messages, respond appropriately: &apos;No messages were found matching your search criteria. Please refine your query and try again.&apos;</description>
            <developerName>SearchSlack_179ak000002zxTS</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>slackAgentSearch</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>standardInvocableAction</invocationTargetType>
